” This is a reflection of the usage of children’s furniture from a consumer.
If the child hides in the cabinet at home for too long, will he feel unwell?
, Or a ventilation opening with equivalent area. Of course, if the child can open the door or open the exit easily when in a confined space, it also adds a guarantee for the child’s safety.
Many consumers are also concerned about the height and size of children’s desks and chairs. For children who are growing fast and have higher posture requirements at the stage of physical development, the choice of desks and chairs is indeed not so easy.
It is not difficult to find in the market that self-adjusting functional desks and chairs are favored by many parents. The matching desks and chairs can adjust their height according to the child’s physical changes, which can meet individual needs and is more convenient.
In a children’s furniture store, a shopping guide pointed out that the frame of the children’s bed should not be too low to prevent the children from rolling off the bed. At the same time, decorative holes should ensure that the child’s limbs can stretch freely to avoid accidents.
In this regard, the “General Technical Requirements for Children’s Furniture” standard requires that children’s furniture should not use glass components in areas within 1600 mm from the ground; if there are dangerous protrusions, they should be protected by appropriate methods. For example, a protective cap or cover is added to effectively increase the area that may be in contact with the skin.
