Bfore you can put your acrylic mirror sheet up, you need to prepare your work area:
• Subtract 3mm from every metre from the dimensions – for example, if the surface was 2m x 8m, you would subtract 6mm from the 3 metre side and 24mm from the 8 metre side. The resulting number is the size that your acrylic sheet needs to be.
• Mark where you need to drill, cut or saw your sheet to make it the correct size. Do this on the protective film, not the acrylic sheet.
• Choose a bonding agent, which could be double-sided tape, acrylic or silicone adhesives. If using tape, place horizontal strips evenly across the width of the acrylic mirror sheet.
• Remove the paper from your double sided tape and hold the top edge of the sheet against your surface at the same 45° angle. Use a spirit level to check that it is straight against the wall, then slowly reduce the sheet’s angle so it lays perfectly flush against the substrate.
• Once the sheet is secured, remove the protective film from the mirrored side that is now facing you.
