Caucasian Shepherd Dog: Know the characteristics, origin and care | Dogs World
Due to environmental conditions has developed a coat capable of protecting it from low temperatures and the most common injuries you may suffer from your herding trade. Its physical complexion is very strong and it is among the largest dogs that exist.
The Russian Kennel Club prefers to use the Russian translation for sheepdog Ovcharka, name with which the breed has also become popular in the western region. The Caucasian Shepherd is part of the renowned trio of Russian shepherds known as the South Russian Shepherd and the Central Asian Shepherd.
The truth is it is a striking ancient breed of unique characteristics. Definitely its origin is from a territory with difficult living conditions, an aspect that allowed the particular genetic development of the breed.
The bites of this dog are among the most powerful in the canine world. This great tool is very useful to your incredibly protective character and determined temperament.
Regarding the physical appearance of Caucasian Shepherd dogs if they are raised correctly they are healthy and long-lived. Regarding their physical complexion, they have strong bones and muscular bodies.
As they are considered giant dogs, it must be assumed that the size of these dogs is quite considerable. Regarding height, the average is 70 centimeters.
Due to their incredible strength and musculature, Caucasian dogs are quite heavy. Females hardly exceed fifty kilos but males can weigh 70 kilos and can even reach 90.
The knowledge of this aspect by the owners is fundamental and due to the function that this dog has fulfilled for centuries defending and guiding livestock, it has innate qualities of a leader. For that reason, its owner has to position himself as the leader of the pack becoming the alpha and for that you must have knowledge.
Although this occurs effectively, it should be known that the Caucasian Shepherd is an animal with strong instincts and if he or his family is considered at risk, he will act as he deems necessary to defend his territory.
It cannot be denied that the Caucasian dog has a reputation for being violent but much of this reputation has been earned by ignorant treatment of this breed, being a great protector of his family. It does what is entrusted to it and fulfills its mission effectively.
It is important to follow the vet's instructions regarding the diet they should follow and the prevention of diseases such hip, elbow and cardiac dysplasia. The latter is greatly influenced by the animal diet, so overweight and obesity should be avoided.
