East dog of chinese origin It is a small specimen that conquers everyone with its graceful appearance and good character. The Shih Tzu is named after the Chinese words 'lion dog', as it was bred to resemble a lion, although its size is far from close to the lion.
6 Why keep a Shih Tzu at home
It will warn the family of the presence of strangers and it will be a brave dog that is willing to defend its own. This does not mean that it is an aggressive dog, but it is strong and loyal.
Their big eyes can cause some problems, so you have to prevent the hair from bothering you. We must clean them if we see that they have dirt and watch them for infections.
The Shih Tzu dog is an animal who is in pretty good health, since their life expectancy is about 13 years. There are a number of diseases that can occur in the dog, such as entropion, progressive retinal atrophy or hip dysplasia.
It's a smart and awake dog it will not take long to learn the orders. It is a breed that can be a bit stubborn, so we must be patient and above all practice daily with them so that they improve their character.
He is a good-natured and sociable dog, but he must still learn to relate. It will be easy for the dog to learn to socialize and be with children and other animals.
Shih Tzu dogs they are charming as soon as you meet them. Their appearance of small stuffed animals makes everyone adore them from the first moment, an impression that is reaffirmed by their good character and playful personality.
