2 How to take your dog in the car
4 Why dog seat belts are useful
The comments point out that the belt is also very resistant, fastens very easily and is a bit elastic.
In case a harness does not interest you and you simply want the strap of the belt, this option from Kurgo is not only simple, with a reasonable price and resistant, is also available in three colors, gray, blue and orange. Thanks to a buckle, the belt can be adjusted so that the dog has more or less room to move, making it very comfortable.
Another model of harness, very comfortable and in the shape of an X, which also includes a belt that you can use in the car. In this case, it is a simpler but also very interesting product that has a practical adjustable strap so that your dog is as comfortable as possible in the back seat.
In addition, it is compatible with a large number of cars, it is available in various colors, it has a very firm carabiner and reflective strips so that you do not lose sight of your pet when it gets dark.
Finally, the last product that we will present today is a double belt for dogs, so if you have two pets it is ideal to take them in the car without the straps getting confused. The material is particularly resistant and has a metal hook for the harness, as well as reflective strips, an elastic part and a single hook for the belt, which is also compatible with most vehicles.
Although the regulations change from country to country, the truth is that both for the safety of our dog and for ours, it is best to carry it well secured in the vehicle.
Carry your dog in the back of the car, behind the front seats. If you have a carrier, it will have to be placed perpendicular to the front seat be it big or small.
In addition, the dog (or the carrier in which we carry it) it also has to be attached to the seat by means of a space harness or some hook like the ones we have just seen so that in the event of a sudden stop or an accident it does not go off and hurt itself.
Why can't the carrier go on top of the seat?
Putting the carrier on the seat attached to the belt is very dangerous, because if there is a sudden stop or jolt, the force causes the belt to break the plastic of the carrier into pieces, which can cause very serious injuries to your poor dog, as well as to the other occupants.
There are many reasons to secure our pet with dog seat belts. (or even better, with a carrier) is an excellent idea to improve the safety of all vehicle occupants:
Nor should we let the dog stick his head out the window or it can be hurt by branches or other objects from outside.
A loose dog is also more likely to distract the driver moving around a lot, barking or even avoiding proper visibility of the road.
Finally, one of the reasons why you should not take the dog in the front seat, in addition to being a distraction for the driver, is that if the airbag is activated it can cause very, very serious injuries.
You can find quite a few different types of dog seat belts in a number of specialty stores.
