The most common straps They are the ones that are made of nylon and they are simply that, a rope to carry hooked to our dog. They are usually available in various sizes and colors and, being the simplest, they are also usually the cheapest.
Leashes for dogs designed for sports They are distinguished by not being retractable, in fact, the vast majority are elastic so you can control your pet (and you don't end up falling). There are those that also incorporate interesting options for humans, for example, a belt to put water or keys, as we saw above.
Finally, elastic straps are very similar to nylon, although they have an internal mechanism that allows the strap to expand a bit, which gives your dog more freedom. It is a type of strap highly recommended for those who go out to do sports or for those who want something halfway between the traditional nylon strap and the retractable one.
When wearing a strap, It is vital that we take into account a series of tips that will help the dog get used to it to the leash and the walks become a pleasure and not a nightmare. For instance:
Just as important is that when putting on the leash, do not adopt threatening poses. Get on your level and, as we said, caress him and speak softly so that he does not panic.
Equally, When you go out the first times, try to make them quiet walks (that is, do not take him to a dog park, for example, where he will find a lot of stimuli that can overwhelm him) and leave him to his air, sniff everything he wants and waste his time.
Finally, if you can, it is better to use a harness instead of a collar. So if the dog throws you, you can control it better and, on top of that, it won't drown.
