What does your pet think about them?
The physical and psychological characteristics are related to both their genetic evolution and the function for which they have been used. The Caucasian Shepherd Dog is native, as its name implies, from the Caucasus region.
Although there are a wide variety of breeds of Caucasian dogs with similar characteristics, currently only one breed is recognized by the name of the Caucasian Shepherd.
The origin of this peculiar dog is still somewhat uncertain and it is rather a rumor that the origin of the breed is considered in the Tibetan Mastiff dog. What is undeniable is that it has been used for a long time as herd keeper and sheepdog thanks to its incredible appearance, strength and resistance to low temperatures.
People who decide to breed this breed of dog must be very well informed about their characteristics, care and needs. If you educate yourself correctly you will have a faithful and protective company.
The nose and nose are compact, its ears are triangular and hang down at the sides and it is currently prohibited to cut off its ears. The head of these pets is large.
The minimum height for males is 65 centimeters and 62 for the female As for the maximum height, there is no stipulated limit. The male is larger and can measure up to 75 centimeters and the females 70.
For an inexperienced owner, raising the pet will be a difficult matter, since the owner must respect and obey by showing control over the animal. If this occurs effectively an unbreakable bond will be created between owner and pet.
For this reason, it is very important that those people who are not related to the animal keep their distance and do not forget that they are facing a powerful bite. The relationship of pets with children is quite harmless considering their nature they simply do not consider them dangerous and neither do their owners.
Among herding duties, a single Caucasian shepherd can handle two wolves that attack the flock. Despite his weight and muscles, they are surprisingly fast and agile and their fur not only protects them from the weather but also from bites, since being thick makes it difficult for the opponent's teeth to reach the skin.
An important aspect is that they need space to spend energyThey are calm and independent and abrupt when it comes to socializing with other races. That is to say, it is not an urban dog since in city spaces it can develop little positive aspects of its character.
Although this animal is quite healthy and does not have hereditary diseases if is susceptible to diseases of large breeds.
Among routine care, vaccines should not be neglected and also it is important to brush it with the appropriate instrument twice a week. Due to its interaction with nature, preventive and timely care must be taken against any type of parasites.
Follow us and you will discover more information about this and other breeds.
