We have designed this product for runners looking for a simple watch with a heart rate monitor on the wrist and a calorie counter.
Heart rate on the wristband (in BPM and % Max HR), stopwatch, calories burnt.
Your maximum heart rate is estimated according to your age and gender. By default, the heart rate at rest is 70 bpm.
If you want to train in a very specific heart rate zone, you can enter a manual heart rate zone into the watch (in BPM or %MHR). A graphic indicator on the screen, along with a sound signal, will inform you when you leave the zone.
The HR 500 watch gives you summaries of your previous runs. For each session, you'll find your run duration, your average heart rate and the number of calories burnt.
The HR 500 jogging watch has a battery life of 2.5 days in heart rate mode and 30.5 days in watch mode. It can be recharged using the USB cable provided.
