Its modular design helps support kids through the Discovering water process with a buoyancy level that reduces as they progress and helps them discover different positions in the water.
Because it is often difficult to find the right buoyancy aid for a kid, to anticipate their level of comfort and confidence in the water, NABAIJI has developed the TISWIM armbands-waistbands. Thanks to its modular design, this adjustable armband-waistband allows your child to discover the joys of playing in the water, moving and learning the first swimming movements in complete safety.
Step 1/ To start with, the TISWIM is used with all of its components (armbands on the arms and the waistband on the front).
Depending on your kid's activity level and duration of sessions in the water, personal buoyancy aids can cause chafing. To prevent this discomfort, we recommend wearing a top underneath the TISWIM adjustable armbands.
How much should I inflate the different parts of the Tiswim?
How can I adjust the inflation of the front section to my kid?
Why does the front section rise to my kid's chin when I use the full product?
Why does my kid end up on their back?
Can my kid fall forward?
It is important to remember that in order to use the adjustable armbands, your kid's motor skills and muscle tone must be sufficiently developed so that they can keep their balance and their head straight when out of the water. However, if your kid moves around a lot and is on the smaller side, adjust the inflation of the front section so that they are a little more submerged at chest level.
In the third stage, your kid can discover the horizontal position in the water with the belt on their back. To do this, fully inflate the back section, without over-inflating it, then position the belt around your kid's waist and tighten normally.
