Our baby gym product designers created these shoes to support your child's psychomotor skills development.
The outsole and the material used on the foot are very flexible.
Between ages one and six, feet play an important role in children's development and growth. Our shoes address the specific needs of children's feet during their many development stages.
From 1 to 2 years (sizes 4 to 7): learning to walk. Feet are flat, round and chubby: our I LEARN shoes are extremely flexible to support children's natural development.From 3 to 6 years (sizes 8 to 11): mastery of walking, running and jumping.
While children's feet do not need shoes to develop, they are important for protection from the cold, damp and impacts, both indoors and out. The Domyos I LEARN shoes give children aged 1 to 2 years the protection they need, while allowing them maximum freedom of movement: flexible shoes let their feet develop naturally, and the thin, flat and flexible outsole provides a sensation of walking barefoot.
Children's feet experience their biggest growth spurt between the ages of 1 and 3. Remember to regularly check their shoe size using our foot gauges in our stores, or on our website on the "Size Guide" page.
As we begin to walk, the arch gradually develops through the natural development of our foot muscles. This is why children's shoes do not need to have an arch support when they are still growing (unless otherwise indicated by a healthcare professional).
What are the mental benefits? Help build self-confidence
