What do this website use your data for?
You can object to this analysis. We will inform you below about how to exercise your options in this regard.
Personal information is any data with which you could be personally identified. This privacy policy explains what information we collect and what we use it for.
The responsible party is the natural or legal person who alone or jointly with others decides on the purposes and means of processing personal data (names, email addresses, etc. ).
Many data processing operations are only possible with your express consent. You may revoke your consent at any time with future effect.
You have the right to have data which we process based on your consent or in fulfillment of a contract automatically delivered to yourself or to a third party in a standard, machine-readable format. If you require the direct transfer of data to another responsible party, this will only be done to the extent technically feasible.
Opposition to promotional emails We hereby expressly prohibit the use of contact data published in the context of website legal notice requirements with regard to sending promotional and informational materials not expressly requested.
Cookies that fall under the "Functionality" category are purely functional and are necessary for the operation of the website or for the implementation of certain functions. Vendors in this category can therefore not be deactivated.
Cookies in the "Usage" category come from providers that provide certain functionalities or content, such as Social media functions, video content, fonts, etc. Providers in this category influence whether all elements on the page work completely.
Cookies in the "Measurement" category come from providers with whom access to the website (of course anonymized) can be analyzed. This provides an overview of website performance and how it evolved.
The website provider automatically collects and stores information that your browser automatically transmits to us in "server log files". These are:
Use of collected data: In addition to the uses mentioned above, the information you provide is used in accordance with the applicable Google data protection policies. Google may publish summary statistics about users' +1 activity or share it with users and partners, such as publishers, advertisers, or affiliate websites.
Google Analytics uses so-called "cookies". These are text files that are stored on your computer and that allow an analysis of the use of the website by you.
We have entered into an agreement with Google for the outsourcing of our data processing and fully implement the strict requirements of the German data protection authorities when using Google Analytics. Demographic data collection by Google Analytics
The information generated by cookies and web beacons relating to your use of this website (including your IP address), and delivery of advertising formats, is transmitted to a Google server in the US and stored there. This information can be passed on from Google to contracting parties of Google.
